# SQL's `FROM` in capitals at the head of a query: a certain fix to `from` (DS0105).
mode: syntax
---- query
FROM orders | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..21
  PIPELINE@0..20
    IDENT@0..4 "FROM"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..11
      IDENT@5..11 "orders"
    WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
    PIPE@12..13 "|"
    WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
    TAKE_OP@14..20
      IDENT@14..18 "take"
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      LITERAL@19..20
        LONG@19..20 "5"
  WHITESPACE@20..21 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `FROM` in capitals
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | FROM orders | take 5
  | ^^^^ keywords are lowercase
  |
  = help: write `from`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from orders | take 5
which parses without errors
